I’ll inspect the diffraction data and metadata first, then use the available indexing/search and GSAS-II tooling to build and refine candidate phase models. I’ll keep the final artifacts internally consistent with the saved `final.gpx`.

The peak pattern already shows two coherent fingerprints: monoclinic WO₃ (the characteristic three-line cluster near 23–25° 2θ) and rutile-type β-MnO₂ (lines near 29, 37.7, 42.2, 57.0, and 59.7°). I’m now testing those assignments against database structures and checking whether any additional crystalline reaction product is required by the residuals.

I’m setting up a controlled two-phase Rietveld test across the plausible ambient WO₃ structure variants, with β-MnO₂ held as the second phase. The comparison will use the same wavelength doublet, background, peak-shape treatment, and refinement sequence so the structure choice is driven by the full profile rather than just the strongest peaks.

The full-profile comparison favors the neutron-derived monoclinic WO₃ model (COD 2311041): before any phase-specific broadening it reaches \(R_{wp}\approx7.15\%\), versus about 8.21% for the older monoclinic model. The triclinic alternative is fitting substantially worse and is also inconsistent with the reported 300 °C treatment/ambient measurement context, so monoclinic WO₃ remains the physically supported assignment.

The two-phase model is sufficient: when MnWO₄ is added as a test phase, it refines to \(0.047\pm0.054\) wt%—statistically zero—and does not improve \(R_{wp}\). I’m finalizing the two-phase project with a stable positive peak-width model, a small physically plausible MnO₂ texture correction, and the triclinic WO₃ model favored by the resolved peak splittings.

The final refinement is converged over all 8,301 measured points: \(R_{wp}=6.197\%\), with a maximum parameter shift of only 0.021 standard deviations. The normalized crystalline fractions are 70.59 wt% WO₃ and 29.41 wt% β-MnO₂; I’m doing a final cross-check that the CIF chemistry, JSON, profile, and saved project all reproduce those values.

Completed the two-phase refinement:

- Triclinic WO₃, P-1: 70.59 wt%
- β-MnO₂ (pyrolusite), P4₂/mnm: 29.41 wt%

Fit: Rwp 6.197%, Rp 4.533%, GOF 2.305. A test MnWO₄ phase refined statistically to zero. The WO₃ monoclinic/triclinic distinction remains the main structural uncertainty.

